          "create_time": 1794811403.786,
          "update_time": 1794811405.469,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The key distinction is emerging: a density’s identity with its own score is generic, while an identity with the fixed theta score may carry real source information. I’m testing whether finitely many of those canonical constraints can distinguish theta from the known controls, and what retaining all of them would require.\n"
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": false,
          "metadata": {
            "source": "Codex completed public message",
