          "create_time": 1794811923.498,
          "update_time": 1794811925.854,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The full canonical score equations do identify the theta measure under explicit integrability assumptions. But the finite defect commutator has a precise gap: the next adjacent defect cancels from its boundary equation. I’m checking whether smooth perturbations can change that missing defect while preserving the retained data and coefficient bound, then submitting the results for a separate internal assessment.\n"
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": false,
          "metadata": {
            "source": "Codex completed public message",
